{"id": "EUVD-2026-72125", "enisaUuid": "d21525cd-60d8-3e48-8cba-c8ac2ebd9135", "description": "nbviewer through 1.0.1 contains a path traversal vulnerability in LocalFileHandler.can_show() that uses string-prefix comparison instead of proper path validation. Attackers can read files from sibling directories outside the configured root by requesting paths that share the root as a textual prefix, disclosing unintended notebooks and credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-09-06T12:37:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-24T14:21:19", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jupyter/nbviewer/issues/1115", "https://github.com/jupyter/nbviewer/blob/1.0.1/nbviewer/providers/local/handlers.py#L92-L107", "https://github.com/jupyter/nbviewer/commit/aad36106f72a1ca7721310c6fccc677ce4c744a5", "https://github.com/jupyter/nbviewer", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nbviewer-through-1.0.1-path-traversal-via-localfilehandler"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v7gx-3h93-r9v6", "CVE-2026-86258"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4f12707e-9a96-3136-a583-ebd383ba89a1", "product": {"name": "nbviewer", "vendor": {"name": "jupyter"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.0.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "21f9a674-a861-3e06-af37-f6b5c7339f87", "vendor": {"name": "jupyter"}}], "isExploited": false}